Phase 2 (FullSpectrum Local-Z, LZ3 batch 1): port the first 5 static
helper functions from FS v0.9.9's PrintObjectSlice.cpp Local-Z planner.

Bottom-up port of the simplest helpers, no FS-only type dependencies
yet. Each one is a tiny standalone utility:

- `bool_from_full_config(cfg, key, fallback)` — read a bool from a
  DynamicPrintConfig, tolerant of ConfigOptionInt for the same key.

- `float_from_full_config(cfg, key, fallback)` — read a coordf_t from
  a DynamicPrintConfig with fallback.

- `segmentation_channel_filament_id(channel_idx)` — MM segmentation
  reserves channel 0 for the parent/default region. Remaining
  channels already line up with 1-based filament IDs.

- `mixed_filament_reference_nozzle_mm(mixed_row, nozzle_diameters)` —
  average of per-component nozzle diameters for a mixed filament row,
  clamped to a 0.05 mm floor.

- `clamped_mixed_component_surface_offset(...)` — resolve per-component
  surface offset for a virtual mixed filament at one layer's print_z,
  then clamp to the per-nozzle maximum so gradient height interpolation
  can't produce physically impossible offsets.

Also: `#include <numeric>` for `std::accumulate`.

DEAD CODE: nothing calls these yet. The build flag list includes
`-Wno-unused-function` so static unused helpers don't error.

Ported from FS v0.9.9 (`ratdoux/OrcaSlicer-FullSpectrum@v0.9.9` commit
b3c41fda), `src/libslic3r/PrintObjectSlice.cpp` lines 873-944.

Verified compile-clean via full libslic3r rebuild (252/252, 0 FAILED)
+ ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug (full APK built).

Continues the Local-Z port started in patch 0044. The remaining ~30
helpers + build_local_z_plan come in subsequent patches; this is the
first cleanly-extracted batch with no FS-only type dependencies.

